WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:07.080
Welcome to the course Conversational AI Concepts, Capabilities, and Use Cases.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:14.720
Think about the last time you interacted with a chat bot at work or as a customer.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.704
Maybe it answered a simple question right away,

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:25.412
or maybe it sent you through a few fixed options and left you feeling stuck when

00:00:25.698 --> 00:00:28.760
your question did not quite fit.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.440
That difference in experience is not accidental.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.394
It comes down to how the conversational system is designed,

00:00:38.419 --> 00:00:43.640
what it is capable of understanding, and how it is implemented.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:50.800
This course focuses on helping you understand those differences

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.300
so you can evaluate Conversational AI solutions with clarity

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.488
and make better decisions in a business context.

00:00:58.488 --> 00:01:01.495
By the end of this course, you will be able to:

00:01:01.495 --> 00:01:04.898
Explain what conversational AI is

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:08.115
and how it differs from traditional automation systems

00:01:08.115 --> 00:01:12.195
such as IVR and rule based chat bots.

00:01:12.195 --> 00:01:18.174
Describe how conversational AI works, including the key technologies

00:01:18.174 --> 00:01:23.916
that enable it to understand input, interpret intent, and generate responses,

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:28.886
and differentiate between traditional chat bots, AI chat bots,

00:01:28.886 --> 00:01:34.273
and agentic AI chat bots, and evaluate implementation approaches

00:01:34.273 --> 00:01:37.893
based on organizational needs and capabilities.